meta {
  name: Create Product No Token
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/product
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Sem Token",
    "description": "Produto criado sem nenhum header de autenticação",
    "price": 9.90,
    "category": "Teste",
    "imageUrl": ""
  }
}

docs {
  No Authorization header at all — tests write access without going through login.

  Expected depends on which environment is selected — this is a KNOWN GAP, not a
  hypothetical (see CLAUDE.md's "Limitações de segurança conhecidas"):
  - "Gateway" (:8080): 401 UNAUTHORIZED, {"error": "Token não fornecido"} — rejected by
    JwtAuthenticationFilter before ever reaching product-service.
  - "ProductDirect" (:8082): 201 CREATED — product-service has no Spring Security
    dependency/config of its own, so it accepts the write unauthenticated. Anyone who
    can reach the container's host-published port bypasses the gateway's ROLE_ADMIN
    check entirely. Clean up the created product afterward if you run this.
}
